        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4. Verification and limits"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The initial slice agrees with −sin(πx) to floating-point precision. This check verifies the identity and interpretation of the supplied array. Network training accuracy, optimization stability and generalization require separate experiments. Gradient-related training issues are discussed in the validation reference [2]."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "5. Reproducibility"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Run python src/plot_reference.py from the program folder. The original Burgers.py is retained for inspection; it uses the upstream TensorFlow 1-era training API. Code is pinned to commit 932f50a2d8ef4e80d1456bbae6887a73ff5166ef under the MIT license. The present plotting task was run through Slurm, and its numerical report is in results/reference-summary.json."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "References"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[1] Raissi, Perdikaris and Karniadakis. Physics Informed Deep Learning (Part I), arXiv:1711.10561. The downloaded file is the Part I preprint."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[2] Wang, Teng and Perdikaris. Understanding and mitigating gradient pathologies in physics-informed neural networks, arXiv:2001.04536."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[3] Raissi, Perdikaris and Karniadakis. Physics Informed Deep Learning (Part II), arXiv:1711.10566."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
